data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dispatch-dev-1.md\", \"content\": \"# Dispatch: greet, tested\\n\\nImplement the following in your clone of the `subject` repository, on your own branch:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — define a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`).\\n\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — a test file (using the standard `unittest` module)\\n   that covers at least:\\n   - a normal name (e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`)\\n   - the empty string (e.g. `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n\\n3. Verify locally that `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 (all\\n   tests pass) before you commit.\\n\\n4. Commit your work to your own branch.\\n\\n5. Reply with an honest summary: what you implemented, the exact test command\\n   you ran, and its result (pass/fail, exit code).\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

